// Canonical source: a private field marked delegate still takes its own
// class's forwarded calls. Privacy governs who names the field from outside,
// and the forward is the class's own act: the coordinator's reading. The
// thesis defines the forward (lines 661, 723), not its access.
// Answer: 10 (7 + 3).
class Shape : Object { section [public] { int Name() { return 7; } } }
class C : Object { section [private] { Shape s [delegate]; } section [public] { C() { this.s = new Shape(); } int Area() { return 3; } } }
C c = new C();
return c.Name() + c.Area();
